WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:03.460
In the trailer for Glass, there are a few
scenes that never showed up in the movie.

00:00:03.460 --> 00:00:07.380
If you want to see which ones, then stick
around to the end of this video.

00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:16.480
Hi, my name is CZ and I created a series called
Things You Missed where I analyse horror movies

00:00:16.480 --> 00:00:19.600
based on some of the things that you might have missed.

00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:21.040
It's pretty self-explanatory.

00:00:21.040 --> 00:00:24.440
As a result of making these episodes, I end
up scrubbing through the trailers a lot to

00:00:24.449 --> 00:00:28.060
find footage -- so I ended up noticing that
there were quite a few scenes in the trailers

00:00:28.060 --> 00:00:29.849
that weren't actually in the movie.

00:00:29.849 --> 00:00:33.660
I decided to look it up and see what info
I could find on this cut content, and ended

00:00:33.660 --> 00:00:37.920
up stumbling on an interview titled, M Night
Shyamalan Reveals Why His First Cut Of Glass

00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:40.010
Was 3 Hours 20 Minutes.

00:00:40.010 --> 00:00:41.120
That's crazy to me.

00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:45.210
I mean, to give you a better idea, the final
runtime was 2 hours and 9 minutes.

00:00:45.210 --> 00:00:47.359
So over an hour of content was cut.

00:00:47.359 --> 00:00:50.250
Not all of that is going to be deleted scenes,
some of it is probably just tightening up

00:00:50.250 --> 00:00:54.519
existing scenes and removing a few of the
24 identities of The Horde, but still, that's

00:00:54.519 --> 00:00:58.660
a lot of footage left on the cutting room...
recycle bin?

00:00:58.660 --> 00:01:01.090
Here's what Shyamalan had to say in the interview.

00:01:01.090 --> 00:01:07.619
"Tons of deleted scenes, I think in retrospect
this was the first time I was writing characters

00:01:07.619 --> 00:01:11.270
that I already knew, so I could write a lot.

00:01:11.270 --> 00:01:12.430
And that's not normal.

00:01:12.430 --> 00:01:14.880
Normally I'm finding them as I'm writing.

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:20.730
And the editing process was what is the essence
of what I needed, so there's a lot of deleted

00:01:20.730 --> 00:01:22.180
scenes for the Blu-Ray and all that stuff."

00:01:22.180 --> 00:01:26.210
With this being our last look into the universe,
the deleted scenes do kind of interest me

00:01:26.210 --> 00:01:30.360
just to get one last look at these characters
we've grown to love, but the Blu-Ray won't

00:01:30.360 --> 00:01:34.780
be out until April -- so that leaves us with
these scenes that are in the trailers.

00:01:34.780 --> 00:01:35.860
Let's take a look at them.

00:01:35.860 --> 00:01:38.301
This is the first one, David sitting in this
restaurant.

00:01:38.301 --> 00:01:41.610
This woman asks him what he does and he tells
her he's in security.

00:01:41.610 --> 00:01:45.189
There's also a slot machine in the corner,
and the TV is broadcasting the opening of

00:01:45.189 --> 00:01:46.320
Osaka Tower.

00:01:46.320 --> 00:01:48.740
I'd theorize that this was meant to be the
opening scene.

00:01:48.740 --> 00:01:51.740
It picks up where David left off in Split,
alone in a diner.

00:01:51.740 --> 00:01:55.460
Not literally the same diner, but symbolically
picking up where we left off.

00:01:55.460 --> 00:01:56.720
And why it was cut?

00:01:56.720 --> 00:02:00.310
If you've seen Unbreakable, you already know
who David is, and we find out about what happened

00:02:00.310 --> 00:02:04.700
to his wife in another scene, so showing him
alone again would really just be redundant.

00:02:04.700 --> 00:02:08.860
Next, we've got this scene of David in his
rain poncho, throwing someone up on a wall.

00:02:08.860 --> 00:02:12.150
It looks like he's in some sort of tunnel
and from what I can tell, he's protecting

00:02:12.150 --> 00:02:15.930
a woman who's been attacked by this criminal;
I think this is a purse right here.

00:02:15.930 --> 00:02:19.480
This probably takes place before the face-off
with The Beast at the factory, and again,

00:02:19.480 --> 00:02:24.040
we already get a good idea of David's life
of vigilante justice in this other scene,

00:02:24.040 --> 00:02:25.340
this scene may not have been needed.

00:02:25.340 --> 00:02:29.459
I do like the symbolic shot composition though,
with the wall colors being yellow and purple,

00:02:29.460 --> 00:02:33.340
the colors of The Horde and Mr. Glass, and
this fence in the foreground telling us that

00:02:33.340 --> 00:02:35.760
David is going to be locked in with these two
enemies.

00:02:35.760 --> 00:02:39.620
In fact it even has the same pattern as the
window on the door to Mr. Glass's room.

00:02:39.620 --> 00:02:42.849
This next one takes place in the final battle
sequence -- it would seem that there's a moment

00:02:42.849 --> 00:02:44.990
where Joseph's wrist is injured at some point.

00:02:44.990 --> 00:02:48.460
It looks like this might be after Casey goes
to try to get Kevin to come into the light,

00:02:48.460 --> 00:02:50.349
because she's not there on the steps with
them.

00:02:50.349 --> 00:02:52.879
So there may have been a beat where the Beast
hurts Joseph.

00:02:52.879 --> 00:02:55.900
I also wouldn't be surprised if the Black
Clover Society was responsible.

00:02:55.900 --> 00:03:00.350
I also have to wonder if part of that hour
of cut content was Joseph questioning if the

00:03:00.350 --> 00:03:05.380
super powers were somehow hereditary... no,
not that Hereditary, and he tries to do something

00:03:05.380 --> 00:03:07.630
that only his father would have been able
to do.

00:03:07.630 --> 00:03:11.549
Perhaps the most mysterious of the deleted
scenes though, is this, where The Beast is

00:03:11.549 --> 00:03:12.800
clutching this woman's head.

00:03:12.800 --> 00:03:14.910
It doesn't appear to be in a violent way though.

00:03:14.910 --> 00:03:18.239
My first thought was that this is Dr. Staple,
but the outfit doesn't seem to match what

00:03:18.239 --> 00:03:21.250
she was wearing after Mr. Glass broke The
Horde out of his room.

00:03:21.250 --> 00:03:24.930
My theory is that there was a scene where
they run into another patient at the institution

00:03:24.930 --> 00:03:28.740
and The Beast, for the same reasons that he
let Casey go at the end of Split, lets her

00:03:28.740 --> 00:03:31.680
go, because he sees that she is broken and
therefore pure.

00:03:31.700 --> 00:03:35.200
We also get a better look at this during
the final trailer, and see that there are

00:03:35.200 --> 00:03:38.760
many people, possibly patients of Raven Hill,
that are reaching out to The Beast in some

00:03:38.770 --> 00:03:40.810
kind of therapeutic ritual.

00:03:40.810 --> 00:03:44.129
There's nothing similar to that in the movie,
so I'd be interested to potentially find out

00:03:44.129 --> 00:03:45.560
what that was going on there.

00:03:45.560 --> 00:03:49.410
Let me know what your theories are about what
was left out the movie, and anything you may

00:03:49.410 --> 00:03:51.840
have noticed from the trailers that didn't
make the cut.

00:03:51.840 --> 00:03:55.860
I'll also be covering the deleted scenes on
Things You Missed when they are released,

00:03:55.860 --> 00:04:00.519
so make sure you're subscribed to CZsWorld
for new horrors every week, ring that deathbell

00:04:00.519 --> 00:04:03.930
for notifications and I'll see you in the
next one.

00:04:03.930 --> 00:04:06.219
Assuming, we both survive.

